    "chunk_text": "With groups like BTS, BLACKPINK, and Stray Kids dominating international charts and breaking records, K-pop\u2019s influence on the global music industry is undeniable.\n\nAlston Koch, now residing in Australia, and Bill Forbes, who migrated to England, are both notable Sri Lankan singers who have made significant contributions to the music industry.\n\nAccording to reports, he has released 21 singles and four albums through record labels like RCA, BMG, EMI, and Sony.\n\nHe has also received many international awards and served as Ambassador for Tourism for Sri Lanka and Ambassador for Climate Change\n\nBill Forbes, considered one of the first Sri Lankan solo artistes to secure a recording contract and achieve a hit recording outside of Sri Lanka, released 16 singles, with his main hit being \u2018Too Young\u2019.\n\nPerhaps our music does blend traditional and modern elements, which can be unique, but it will not appeal to a broader global audience without adaptation or fusion with international styles.\n\nTo bridge this gap, our folks need to work with artistes from other countries, or genres, to create fusion music that appeals to a broader audience.\n\nIf we don\u2019t do it differently, like K-pop, our artistes will remain unknown in the scene that matters \u2026 only catering to Sri Lankans, even when they embark on overseas tours,\n\nLeave a Reply Cancel replyYour email address will not be published. Required fields are marked *Comment * Name *\n\nSave my name, email, and website in this browser for the next time I comment."
