    "md5": "5139accfa43b6464b1bfc10168bfebf9",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1599,
    "chunk_text": "ADB team visits MAS Holdings\u2019 Fabric Park in Sri Lanka\n\nECONOMYNEXT \u2013 An Asian Development Bank (ADB) delegation visited MAS Holdings\u2019 Fabric Park in Thulhiriya, Sri Lanka as part of its efforts to support the private sector through partnerships and investment.\n\nThe visit offered the ADB team an opportunity to experience MAS\u2019 operations firsthand and gain insights into the company\u2019s commitment to manufacturing excellence and sustainable business practices, the company said in a statement.\n\n\u201cPartnerships with leading private sector companies like MAS are essential to driving sustainable growth and resilience. We are encouraged by the company\u2019s commitment to innovation and environmental stewardship, which align strongly with ADB\u2019s development priorities in the region,\u201d said Takafumi Kadono, Country Director of ADB for Sri Lanka.\n\n\u201cTheir visit reflects the growing importance of institutions like the Asian Development Bank in understanding the evolving dynamics of the apparel industry in Sri Lanka,\u201d Rajitha Jayasuriya, Director \u2013 Corporate Affairs said.\n\n\u201cMeaningful engagement like this helps build bridges between industry and development partners, unlocking new pathways for inclusive growth and long-term impact.\u201d\n\nBy connecting with a leading development institution such as ADB, MAS highlights the potential for specialised investments, knowledge sharing, and strategic partnerships that can strengthen Sri Lanka\u2019s apparel sector, the company said.\n\nSri Lanka\u2019s apparel industry is a key driver of employment and export revenue. (Colombo/Sep10/2025)"
