    "md5": "0917bf3110bf6d1d5e2882ecd6806bef",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 666,
    "chunk_text": "It is also unfortunate that the JVP, in attempting to satisfy hardliners, is repeating a historical misstep. Originally, the party opposed Indian involvement and the 13th Amendment (13A), fighting against perceived external interference. Today, by rejecting or delaying devolution mechanisms, they risk undermining the utility of 13A\u2014not just for the North and East, but for the country as a whole. In practice, the amendment\u2019s provisions are more significant for the majority population in the South. Historically, Western Province alone has introduced more than 70 statutes under devolution powers, demonstrating the potential of empowered provincial councils."
