    "md5": "ae2c43094db7322158360348c116150b",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1985,
    "chunk_text": "There has been a far more serious claim about a conspiracy here. In 2022, the then Speaker Mahinda Yaha Abeywardena told Parliament that there had been a conspiracy to pressure him to appoint himself as the Acting President in violation of the Constitution at the height of a popular uprising that led to democratically elected President Gotobaya Rajapaksa to flee the country and resign.\n\nLeader of the National Freedom Front Wimal Weerawansa was the first to claim that there had been a foreign conspiracy to oust President Gotabaya Rajapaksa and Prime Minister Mahinda Rajapaksa. He said the US had been party to it. US Ambassador Julie Chung rejected his claim out of hand.\n\nWhat we witnessed in Colombo, on 09 July 2022, has been viewed in some quarters as the culmination of a well-planned destabilisation process aimed at shaking this country off the sphere of influence of one world power and realigning it with some others. If Parliament had fallen into the hands of violent protesters who went all out to march on it, the country would have been plunged into anarchy like Libya. Gotabaya himself blamed his ouster on a conspiracy.\n\nAbeywardena\u2019s claim that some local and foreign individuals hatched a plot to plunge this country into anarchy has gone unprobed while Bolsonaro has been jailed for a coup he plotted in the same year. If those who attempted to force Abeywardena to resort to an illegal course of action had succeeded in their endeavour, this country would have descended into anarchy. There is no guarantee that the same sinister forces will not make a fresh attempt to achieve their goal, and create conditions for another uprising. Hence the need for Abeywardena\u2019s claim to be investigated thoroughly and action taken against those who were behind the 2022 \u2018conspiracy\u2019. It may be recalled that ousted Prime Minister of Bangladesh Sheikh Hasina has also alleged that there was a foreign hand behind the uprising that toppled her government last year."
  },
