    "chunk_text": "Sri Lanka Secure Second Victory in T20 Asia Cup 2025\n\nCOLOMBO (News 1st): Sri Lanka secured their second win of the 2025 Men\u2019s T20 Asia Cup after defeating Hong Kong by four wickets in Dubai.Winning the toss, skipper Charith Asalanka opted to bowl first.\u00a0Hong Kong\u2019s innings saw their first wicket fall at 41 runs.\u00a0Zeeshan Ali contributed 23 runs, while Anshy Rath produced a spirited 48.\u00a0The standout performer was Nizakat Khan, who top-scored with 52 off 38 deliveries.\u00a0For Sri Lanka, Dushmantha Chameera claimed two wickets, while Wanindu Hasaranga and Dasun Shanaka picked up one wicket each.\u00a0Hong Kong closed their innings at 149 for 4.In response, Sri Lanka\u2019s chase began with Pathum Nissanka and Kusal Mendis.\u00a0Mendis was dismissed early for 11, while Kamil Mishara added 19.\u00a0Nissanka anchored the innings brilliantly, smashing 68 off just 44 balls, including 6 fours and 2 sixes.Chasing 150, Sri Lanka reached the target in 18.5 overs, finishing at 150 for 6, securing a four-wicket victory.This win strengthens Sri Lanka\u2019s position in the group stage as they continue their campaign in the Asia Cup 2025."
