    "chunk_text": "Sri Lanka bond yields drop following US Fed rate cut, rupee stronger\n\nECONOMYNEXT \u2013 Sri Lanka\u2019s secondary market bond yields dropped following the US Federal Reserve rate cut announcement, dealers said, while the rupee appreciated to 301.90/302.00 against the dollar.\n\nAmong the actively traded bonds, a bond maturing on 15.12.2029 was seen trading lower at 9.50/54 percent from the previous closing 9.55/60 percent.\n\nA bond maturing on 15.03.2031 was quoted at 10.00/02 percent.\n\nA bond maturing on 15.12.2032 was quoted at 10.35/45 percent, from 10.40/49 percent.\n\nThe telegraphic transfer rates for the American dollar was 298.5000 buying, 305.5000 selling; the British pound was 405.7748 buying, and 417.1366 selling, and the euro was 350.6062 buying, 361.9694 selling.\n\nThe Colombo Stocks Exchange was trading in green; The ASPI was up 0.63 percent, or 131.18 points, at 20,906; the S&P SL20 was down 0.82 percent, or 48.29 points, at 5,951.(Colombo/Sep18/2025)."
