    "chunk_size_bytes": 1513,
    "chunk_text": "It\u2019s a big question\n\nSome government leaders\u2019 asset declarations, submitted to the Commission to Investigate Allegations of Bribery and Corruption, are now in the public domain. They have become grist for the Opposition\u2019s mill. The political rivals of the ruling JVP-led NPP are in overdrive, trying to depict the JVP leaders as a bunch of hypocrites who have enriched themselves while pretending to be dependent on financial assistance from their \u2018Marxist\u2019 party even to satisfy their basic needs. But these critics have chosen to ignore the fact that some key Opposition politicians have not yet submitted their asset declarations.\n\nThe assets of JVP full-timers, such as President Anura Kumara Dissanayake, Ministers Wasantha Samarasinghe and Bimal Rathnayake and Deputy Minister Sunil Watagala, have received much media attention. The Opposition is using them to dispute the JVP\u2019s claim that its leaders are part of the proletariat and sharing in the economic hardships of the masses. The asset declarations submitted by some Opposition figures, including Namal Rajapaksa, too, have raised many eyebrows.\n\nCuriously, most of the politicians with assets that ordinary people can only dream of acquiring are without any known sources of income. Some of them say they have inherited wealth, and their claims remind us of Daisy  Aachchi\u2019s bag of gems. How they have amassed so much wealth is a big question. Politics has obviously become El Dorado for many individuals across the political spectrum."
