    "md5": "f4907c449c05cfccaad0a8cb5875b065",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1672,
    "chunk_text": "With over 20 years of senior leadership across diverse industries, Prematillake, one of Sri Lanka\u2019s leading corporate personalities, currently serves as the Managing Director of Hayleys Fentons Ltd. and its subsidiaries, bringing deep expertise and strategic vision.\n\nPrematillake spearheaded a remarkable transformation at Hayleys Fentons, steering the company from a Rs. 600 million loss and a negative equity of Rs. 1.4 billion in 2019 to achieving over Rs. 3 billion in profit and building an equity base exceeding Rs. 5 billion. Under his leadership, the company rose to rank among the top five performers within the Hayleys Group. Navigating through three major crises, the Easter attacks in 2019, the global pandemic in 2020, and Sri Lanka\u2019s economic turbulence in 2022, he implemented agile strategies that streamlined operations, enhanced cash flow, strengthened talent development, and ensured sustained profitability through strong financial stewardship and adaptability.\n\nGuided by Prematillake\u2019s sustainability-first vision, Hayleys Fentons has become a vanguard of renewable energy in Sri Lanka. Hayleys Solar, the company\u2019s flagship energy venture, now leads the market and is on track to become the first local company to achieve over 500 MW in installed capacity by the end of 2025, focusing on utility-scale solar and innovative solar solutions that enhance land productivity and sustainable agriculture. He has also led the company\u2019s successful bid for Sri Lanka\u2019s largest wind power plant, expanded regional operations and advanced battery storage and circular energy solutions through strategic partnerships and inclusive financing models."
  },
