    "chunk_size_bytes": 1280,
    "chunk_text": "The ties between the two democracies are still evolving. As a member-state of the European Union, Poland is increasingly attractive to Sri Lankan professionals. As of the end of 2024, approximately 1,600 Sri Lankans worked in Poland. These statistics may not be impressive; however, over the last decade the number of Sri Lankan workers in Poland has increased nearly 30-fold.\n\nIn this process, I had the opportunity to give lectures at General Sir John Kotelawala Defence University and the Royal Asiatic Society of Sri Lanka. I am also deeply honored to be invited as a keynote speaker to the 46th National Conference of Chartered Accountants of Sri Lanka that will take place on October 8\u201310 in Sri Jayewardenepura Kotte.\n\nIt is our hope to strengthen the ties between Sri Lanka and Poland\u2014going far beyond tea and tourism.\n\n*Dr. Antonina Luszczykiewicz-Mendis, a visiting scholar at the University of Oxford, is an assistant professor at the Jagiellonian University in Krakow, Poland.\n\nRanil\u2019s Triple-R Programme \u2013 Relief, Rehabilitation and Reconciliation \u2013 and work style\n\nLeave a Reply Cancel replyYour email address will not be published. Required fields are marked *Comment * Name *\n\nSave my name, email, and website in this browser for the next time I comment."
