    "chunk_index": 3,
    "language": "en",
    "md5": "0aa5769ada0333d7efbfa0d3be83b1ca",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 559,
    "chunk_text": "To paint Ravana as flawless would be as misguided as portraying him purely as evil. He was proud, perhaps even vengeful. But he was also loyal, learned, and by many accounts, honorable even in enmity. And that is what makes him profoundly human.\n\nIn revisiting Ravana, we are not just retelling a myth. We are reclaiming a memory. We are recognizing that mythology is not fixed, it is alive, shaped by who tells it, when, and why. And sometimes, the most important act of justice we can perform for a maligned figure is to simply ask: what if we got it wrong?"
