    "md5": "a2c50c0aa4a743f4a6defe8ee899b611",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 2014,
    "chunk_text": "Nawaloka silences its critics, marks 40 years of resilience\n\nAmid a backdrop of social media speculation and doubts about its financial viability earlier in the year, Nawaloka Hospitals PLC has responded not with words, but with a powerful statement of legacy and future-proofing: a grand celebration of its 40th anniversary.\n\nChoosing to ignore the negative commentary that circulated in the recent past, the management remained focused on its long-term vision. That vision was on full display on September 18th as the pioneering private healthcare institution unveiled a special 40th-anniversary logo and a commemorative postage stamp, marking four decades of medical excellence since its establishment in 1985.\n\nThe event, attended by the hospital\u2019s leadership, consultants, and staff, served as a robust testament to the institution\u2019s stability and enduring commitment. The new logo, in the auspicious colours for 2026, symbolizes a refreshed brand identity focused on progress, trust, and continuity.\n\nChairman Dr. Jayantha Dharmadasa underscored this commitment, stating the anniversary is a \u201cpromise to continue advancing healthcare by caring, leading, and healing with feeling.\u201d This forward-looking vision was further emphasised with plans to deeply integrate Artificial Intelligence (AI) into operations to enhance patient care and medical research.\n\nBy celebrating a landmark 40-year journey of pioneering complex procedures and \u201cHealing with Feeling,\u201d Nawaloka Hospitals has effectively let its legacy and ambitious plans for the future silence its critics, demonstrating that its foundation is as solid as ever.\n\nS&P Global Ratings upgrade boosts bourse but debt burden blights recovery prospects\n\nSri Lanka Tourism can\u2019t move forward on old wheels; the answer lies with Finance Ministry: CTGLA\n\nLeave a Reply Cancel replyYour email address will not be published. Required fields are marked *Comment * Name *\n\nSave my name, email, and website in this browser for the next time I comment."
