    "chunk_size_bytes": 1707,
    "chunk_text": "Power of criminals\n\nA huge consignment of narcotics and several illegal firearms, including an assault rifle, were detected in Tangalle on Monday. They would possibly have gone undetected if not for the suspicious death of a person that led the police to a place where a truck used to transport some of the narcotics was parked. Two other persons were found dead on the scene. Later on, the police took into custody two other trucks with narcotics and illegal firearms.\n\nIt is incumbent upon the police to conduct a separate investigation to find out how the drug haul and illegal firearms had been smuggled into the country. There have been prima facie lapses on the part of the authorities tasked with battling the narco menace, and they should be probed so that the police will have a better understanding of the clandestine operations of the drug Mafia, which employs very innovative methods to accomplish their missions.\n\nSome trawlers are used for drug smuggling and gun running, as is public knowledge. Coastal areas in the South have come to be plagued by bloody turf wars, some of which have been going on for years. Keeping fishing harbours and trawlers under surveillance is a prerequisite for holding many drug smugglers at bay.\n\nThe controversial practice of releasing freight containers via the green channel has stood drug dealers and other smugglers in good stead, and it must be abandoned forthwith. If the Customs and the police get their act together, the goal of ridding the country of drugs will be within the realm of possibility. They should be given all necessary resources and a free hand. The strength of the Navy must not be reduced on any grounds. Instead, it should be enhanced."
